## Environment Variables

You can easily add and enforce validation for your own custom environment variables:

1. Add your custom variable in your local `.env` file:
   ```env
   MY_CUSTOM_API_KEY="your-api-key-here"
   ```
2. Open `src/config.ts` and add its validation schema to the `envSchema` property using `zod`:
   ```typescript
   export const config = new Config({
     // ...
     envSchema: z.object({
       MY_CUSTOM_API_KEY: z.string(),
     }),
     // ...
   })
   ```
3. Use it securely and with full TypeScript typing inside your code by importing it from the core module:
   ```typescript
   import env from "#core/env"

   console.log(env.MY_CUSTOM_API_KEY) // Strongly-typed string!
   ```

